WEBVTT

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.976
Brother John Bates

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.969
is that not the morning
which breaks yonder?

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.982
I think it be.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:22.012
But we have no great cause
to desire the approach of day.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.322
Who's there?!

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.656
A friend.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.992
Under what Captain serve you?

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.362
Under Sir Thomas Erpingham.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:41.668
I pray you,
what thinks he of our estate?

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.539
Even as men wrecked upon a sand

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.170
that look to be washed off
at the next tide.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.511
He hath not told
his thought to the king?

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.017
No.
Nor it is not meet he should.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:55.021
For though I speak it to you

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:59.549
I think the king is...
but a man, as I am.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.459
The violet smells to him

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.395
as it doth to me.

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:07.958
In his nakedness,
he appears but a man.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:11.493
Therefore his fears,
out of doubt

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:15.133
be of the same relish
as ours are.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:18.474
Yet, no man should possess him
with any appearance of fear

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.912
Iest he, by showing it,
should dishearten his army.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.473
He may show
what outward courage he will

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.109
but I believe,
as cold a night as 'tis

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.211
he could wish himself in Thames
up to the neck.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.815
Methinks I could not
die anyplace so contented

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.656
as in the king's company.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.855
His cause being just

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.523
and his quarrel honorable.

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.157
That's more than we know.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.327
Or more than we
should seek after.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.199
If his cause be wrong

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:47.365
our obedience to the king
wipes the crime of it out of us.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:50.342
But if the cause be not good

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.844
the king, himself, have
a heavy reckoning to make

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.347
when all those legs and arms and
heads chopped off in a battle

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.509
shall join together
at the latter day and cry all

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.212
"We died at such a place."

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.948
The king is not bound to answer

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.956
the particular endings
of his soldiers

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.217
the father of his son

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.453
nor the master of his servant.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.223
Splendid, Data, splendid.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.457
You're getting
better and better.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:12.988
Freeze program.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.294
Thank you, sir.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:21.967
I plan to study the performances
of Olivier

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.975
Branagh, Shapiro and Kullnark.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:24.999
Data...

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.502
You're here to learn

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.640
about the human condition.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.082
And there is no better way
of doing that

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.983
than by embracing Shakespeare.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.979
But... you must discover it
through your own performance

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.322
not by imitating others.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.987
Riker to Picard.
Sorry to interrupt, sir.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.325
Go ahead, Number One.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.955
Sensors are picking up

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.296
a unidentified craft
in the Neutral Zone.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.494
It's heading toward
Federation space.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.003
We're on our way.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.334
Picard out.

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:55.500
We'll get to the rest of the act
another time, Data.

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.533
Computer, file program
and clear.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.847
Captain, why should a king

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.644
wish to pass as a commoner?

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:06.675
If he is the leader,
should he not be leading?

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.277
Listen to what Shakespeare

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.949
is telling you
about the man, Data.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:14.448
A king who had true
feeling for his soldiers

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.962
would wish to share
their fears with them

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.964
on the eve of battle.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.966
Sir, will I be able to schedule

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.969
a performance for the crew
in the near future?

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.471
Let's not rush it, shall we?

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:27.803
Hmm.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:38.408
Outpost Sierra Vl
confirms our readings, sir.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.851
They identify it
as a Romulan scoutship.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:41.979
Bearing: 270 mark 14.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.818
Scoutship.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.757
What would a scoutship be doing
this far into the Neutral Zone?

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:47.953
Captain, shall we transmit

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.359
a warning to withdraw, sir?

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.987
Open a hailing frequency.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.327
Aye, sir.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:54.993
Captain, the Romulan
is hailing us.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.331
Visual.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.836
Not within range, yet.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.497
Open a channel.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.598
Federation ship, do you read?

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.609
I require urgent assistance.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:06.942
This is Captain Jean-Luc Picard
of the USS...

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.278
Federation ship, please help me.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.612
Requesting asylum.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.947
Under pursuit.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.452
Pursuit?

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.783
Visual range.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.311
On screen, Captain.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:56.327
Space, the final frontier.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:05:00.196
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:02.200
Its continuing mission--

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:06.170
to explore strange new worlds

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:10.642
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:15.170
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:06:18.009 --> 00:06:19.237
Red Alert.

00:06:19.277 --> 00:06:20.539
Open a channel to the warship.

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:21.637
Come to intercept course.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.045
Keep us out of the Neutral Zone.

00:06:23.081 --> 00:06:24.412
Channel is open.

00:06:24.449 --> 00:06:27.077
How long before they cross over
into Federation territory?

00:06:27.118 --> 00:06:28.449
41 Seconds, sir.

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:29.454
Romulan warbird

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:31.581
this is Captain Jean-Luc Picard

00:06:31.623 --> 00:06:33.750
of the Federation vessel
Enterprise.

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:36.090
You have crossed
into the Neutral Zone

00:06:36.127 --> 00:06:38.425
and are engaged
in hostile action.

00:06:38.463 --> 00:06:40.761
Explain yourself
and your intent.

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:42.426
No reply, sir.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:43.764
Hail the scout.

00:06:43.802 --> 00:06:45.429
Responding.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:46.767
On screen.

00:06:46.805 --> 00:06:48.272
Federation craft...

00:06:48.306 --> 00:06:51.070
please, you must help me!

00:06:51.109 --> 00:06:53.100
We are moving to intercept.

00:06:53.144 --> 00:06:54.941
Maintain your course and power.

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:02.050
The scoutship
is severely damaged, sir.

00:07:02.087 --> 00:07:04.214
Engines inoperative,
shields are down.

00:07:04.256 --> 00:07:05.553
Position?

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.058
Coordinates 140 by 205, sir.

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:09.390
Federation space.

00:07:09.427 --> 00:07:11.054
Right. Move to within
five kilometers.

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:14.429
Mr. La Forge, prepare to extend

00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:16.093
our shields
around the Romulan scoutship.

00:07:16.134 --> 00:07:17.931
At that range, the shields
won't be able to take

00:07:18.036 --> 00:07:19.025
much punishment, Captain.

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:20.401
Five kilometers, sir.

00:07:20.438 --> 00:07:22.065
All stop.

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:23.574
Extend shields.

00:07:23.608 --> 00:07:25.075
Shields in place.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.271
We've got the scoutship,
Captain.

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:39.586
The weapons on the warbird
are fully powered, sir.

00:07:39.624 --> 00:07:41.751
Lock phasers.
Open a channel.

00:07:41.793 --> 00:07:43.090
Ready.

00:07:43.128 --> 00:07:44.390
Romulan vessel

00:07:44.429 --> 00:07:46.920
you are now
in Federation territory.

00:07:46.965 --> 00:07:49.559
Unless you withdraw...

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:52.092
No argument?

00:07:52.137 --> 00:07:55.595
Warbird has re-entered
the Neutral Zone.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:57.540
Heading
toward Romulan territory.

00:07:57.576 --> 00:08:00.545
Massive power failure
to the scoutship, sir.

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:02.103
All systems are going off-line

00:08:02.147 --> 00:08:03.375
including life-support.

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:04.905
Transporter 2, prepare to beam

00:08:04.983 --> 00:08:07.474
the occupant of the scoutship
directly aboard.

00:08:07.519 --> 00:08:08.486
Aye, sir.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.487
Mr. Worf.

00:08:09.521 --> 00:08:12.388
Mr. Data,
lock onto the scoutship.

00:08:12.424 --> 00:08:14.415
Take it in tow.

00:08:17.362 --> 00:08:18.590
Energize.

00:08:33.445 --> 00:08:35.345
I must see your Captain
immediately.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:36.938
We'll get you to Sick Bay.

00:08:37.048 --> 00:08:37.946
After that...

00:08:38.049 --> 00:08:39.414
This cannot wait!

00:08:39.451 --> 00:08:42.614
I have information
vital to your survival.

00:08:46.524 --> 00:08:50.620
Captain's Log, Stardate 43462.5.

00:08:50.662 --> 00:08:53.961
We have beamed aboard
an apparent Romulan defector

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:57.162
who claims to be
a low-ranking logistics officer

00:08:57.202 --> 00:09:00.933
with extraordinary information
about a secret offensive.

00:09:00.972 --> 00:09:03.304
The humiliating defeat
at the battle of Cheron

00:09:03.341 --> 00:09:04.899
has not been forgotten.

00:09:04.943 --> 00:09:08.140
The new leaders have vowed
to disregard the treaty

00:09:08.179 --> 00:09:10.010
and claim the Neutral Zone.

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:12.141
Nelvana lll is just
the first step.

00:09:12.183 --> 00:09:13.548
You're saying an entire base

00:09:13.585 --> 00:09:15.314
has already been
established there?

00:09:15.353 --> 00:09:19.153
Within 48 hours, the reactor
core will be on-line.

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:22.785
So the Federation sensors
that monitor the Neutral Zone

00:09:22.827 --> 00:09:23.919
just missed it.

00:09:24.029 --> 00:09:26.497
It would seem so.

00:09:26.531 --> 00:09:33.164
In two days,
a fleet of Romulan warbirds

00:09:33.204 --> 00:09:35.934
will be within
striking distance

00:09:36.007 --> 00:09:38.339
of 15 Federation sectors.

00:09:38.376 --> 00:09:39.843
The Federation
will not permit that.

00:09:39.878 --> 00:09:44.144
Then it is war that we're
talking about, isn't it?

00:09:45.884 --> 00:09:50.947
Destroy the base now
and the threat is over.

00:09:51.022 --> 00:09:54.753
Well, I'm sure you are fatigued
by your ordeal

00:09:54.793 --> 00:09:56.761
and you require
medical attention.

00:09:56.795 --> 00:09:58.092
Lieutenant Worf

00:09:58.129 --> 00:10:00.962
will you conduct Sublieutenant
Setal to the Sick Bay?

00:10:00.999 --> 00:10:02.864
We will attend

00:10:02.901 --> 00:10:03.959
to your quarters.

00:10:04.035 --> 00:10:07.095
No doubt you will wish
to question me further.

00:10:08.973 --> 00:10:10.440
No doubt.

00:10:23.221 --> 00:10:24.688
He tells a hell of a story.

00:10:24.723 --> 00:10:26.315
You don't believe it.

00:10:26.357 --> 00:10:28.985
Well, the Empire knows
that we would never allow them

00:10:29.027 --> 00:10:31.427
to build a base
within the Neutral Zone.

00:10:31.463 --> 00:10:34.296
Commander, that would not be
an atypical Romulan ploy.

00:10:34.332 --> 00:10:36.129
In their long history of war

00:10:36.167 --> 00:10:38.226
the Romulans have
rarely attacked first.

00:10:38.269 --> 00:10:40.999
They prefer to test
their enemy's resolve.

00:10:41.106 --> 00:10:42.539
I think he's a plant

00:10:42.574 --> 00:10:44.337
to draw us
into the Neutral Zone.

00:10:44.375 --> 00:10:46.400
That way, we look
like the aggressors.

00:10:46.444 --> 00:10:47.877
And the Romulans would have

00:10:47.912 --> 00:10:50.278
a legitimate excuse
for responding in force.

00:10:50.315 --> 00:10:51.282
Exactly.

00:10:51.316 --> 00:10:52.544
That would also

00:10:52.584 --> 00:10:54.484
not be an atypical
Romulan ploy, sir.

00:10:54.519 --> 00:10:58.387
It's always a game of chess
with them, isn't it?

00:10:58.423 --> 00:11:00.288
Well, at least he's given us

00:11:00.325 --> 00:11:01.724
a chance to get a look

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.092
at some Romulan
technology close-up.

00:11:04.129 --> 00:11:07.223
Mr. La Forge, you will lead
the away team over to the scout.

00:11:07.265 --> 00:11:09.392
Commander,
you and Counselor Troi

00:11:09.434 --> 00:11:11.425
will conduct Setal's
interrogation.

00:11:11.469 --> 00:11:14.267
Captain, permission to
observe the interrogation.

00:11:14.305 --> 00:11:15.670
No, Mr. Data.

00:11:15.707 --> 00:11:16.867
I need you
on the Bridge with me.

00:11:16.908 --> 00:11:17.966
There is much to be done.

00:11:18.009 --> 00:11:21.342
We have less than 48 hours
to prevent a war

00:11:21.379 --> 00:11:23.711
or, perhaps...

00:11:23.748 --> 00:11:25.943
to start one.

00:11:25.984 --> 00:11:27.417
This will depend

00:11:27.452 --> 00:11:28.851
on establishing the truth...

00:11:36.127 --> 00:11:38.254
I set
the autodestruct sequencer

00:11:38.296 --> 00:11:40.287
before I left the ship.

00:11:40.331 --> 00:11:41.298
Why?

00:11:41.332 --> 00:11:42.799
Wouldn't you?

00:11:42.833 --> 00:11:46.200
To prevent your ship
from being captured?

00:11:46.237 --> 00:11:47.898
Excuse me for being
a little confused, Setal

00:11:47.938 --> 00:11:49.200
but I thought
you were defecting.

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:51.208
I am not a traitor.

00:11:51.242 --> 00:11:57.806
All you can see is
the opportunity to exploit me.

00:11:57.848 --> 00:12:01.284
The Federation credo--
exploitation!

00:12:01.319 --> 00:12:03.719
Oh, you couldn't get aboard
my ship fast enough, hmm?

00:12:03.754 --> 00:12:06.951
Strip it down.

00:12:07.058 --> 00:12:11.154
"What secrets might it reveal
that we can use?"

00:12:11.195 --> 00:12:13.686
You're shortsighted people.

00:12:13.731 --> 00:12:15.596
Can't you understand?

00:12:15.633 --> 00:12:17.464
I came to stop a war.

00:12:17.501 --> 00:12:21.403
If you could just hold still.

00:12:23.407 --> 00:12:24.772
With your metabolism

00:12:24.809 --> 00:12:27.801
this will heal in a few moments.

00:12:33.484 --> 00:12:35.975
Thank you, Doctor.

00:12:36.087 --> 00:12:37.281
How fortunate

00:12:37.321 --> 00:12:39.949
that you know something
of Romulan medicine.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:43.221
Yes, I had a chance to gain

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.852
some experience recently.

00:12:44.895 --> 00:12:45.862
Oh, yes.

00:12:45.896 --> 00:12:48.126
The incident
at the Galorndon Core.

00:12:48.165 --> 00:12:49.792
The two officers.

00:12:49.834 --> 00:12:53.964
You are aware of a great deal
for a logistics clerk.

00:12:56.107 --> 00:12:59.008
It was common knowledge.

00:12:59.043 --> 00:13:02.535
I could show you my rating code.

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:06.539
Forged credentials are
a simple matter for a spy.

00:13:06.584 --> 00:13:10.680
How do you allow Klingon pahtk

00:13:10.721 --> 00:13:14.782
to walk around
in a Starfleet uniform?

00:13:14.825 --> 00:13:18.420
You are lucky
this is not a Klingon ship.

00:13:18.462 --> 00:13:20.430
We know how to deal with spies.

00:13:20.464 --> 00:13:22.694
Remove this tohzah
from my sight.

00:13:22.733 --> 00:13:25.293
Your knowledge of Klingon curses

00:13:25.336 --> 00:13:26.496
is impressive

00:13:26.537 --> 00:13:30.303
but, as a Romulan might say,
only a veruul would use

00:13:30.341 --> 00:13:31.968
such language in public.

00:13:32.042 --> 00:13:33.202
Mr. Worf

00:13:33.244 --> 00:13:35.872
please see
to the security arrangements

00:13:35.913 --> 00:13:37.505
for our guest's stay.

00:13:37.548 --> 00:13:39.311
Aye, sir.

00:13:44.488 --> 00:13:47.616
You find something amusing?

00:13:47.658 --> 00:13:49.785
Lieutenant Worf-- I like him.

00:13:49.827 --> 00:13:52.955
To be more accurate,
I understand him--

00:13:52.997 --> 00:13:54.988
a warrior, proud

00:13:55.099 --> 00:13:59.399
fearless,
living only for combat.

00:13:59.437 --> 00:14:02.736
Exactly the type
that will get us all killed

00:14:02.773 --> 00:14:05.401
if we're not careful.

00:14:18.321 --> 00:14:20.619
This is the food station.

00:14:20.656 --> 00:14:23.955
You can reach me
through the com panel.

00:14:23.993 --> 00:14:25.620
Later, we would like

00:14:25.661 --> 00:14:28.323
to ask you
a few more questions.

00:14:32.535 --> 00:14:34.298
Computer, water.

00:14:34.337 --> 00:14:35.964
Temperature?

00:14:36.072 --> 00:14:37.300
12 onkians.

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:41.299
This system is calibrated
to the Celsius metric system.

00:14:41.344 --> 00:14:42.811
Any temperature at all

00:14:42.845 --> 00:14:45.643
on the cold side
of whatever your system is.

00:15:22.485 --> 00:15:26.512
There is no unusual activity
in the Nelvana system, sir.

00:15:26.555 --> 00:15:30.491
Let's isolate
and magnify that system.

00:15:30.526 --> 00:15:33.256
Nothing on the sensors.

00:15:35.665 --> 00:15:40.329
It's hard to believe
in what one cannot see

00:15:40.369 --> 00:15:45.500
and yet, conceivably,
with their cloaking technology

00:15:45.541 --> 00:15:47.304
a fleet of Romulan warbirds

00:15:47.343 --> 00:15:50.312
could be passing
before our eyes.

00:15:50.346 --> 00:15:53.941
There must be some way
to neutralize this advantage.

00:15:53.983 --> 00:15:57.976
Captain Picard, priority one
message from Starfleet

00:15:58.054 --> 00:15:59.988
coming in on secured channel.

00:16:00.056 --> 00:16:01.580
In my ready room.

00:16:01.624 --> 00:16:03.251
Computer, delay time?

00:16:03.292 --> 00:16:06.090
Two hours, 22 minute delay
from time of transmission

00:16:06.128 --> 00:16:08.961
at Starfleet Command on Lya lll.

00:16:13.135 --> 00:16:16.468
Computer, key access
412 mark 80.

00:16:16.505 --> 00:16:17.665
Picard, Jean-Luc.

00:16:17.707 --> 00:16:19.868
Starfleet priority code Gamma.

00:16:19.909 --> 00:16:21.342
Decode.

00:16:21.377 --> 00:16:23.607
Begin message.

00:16:23.646 --> 00:16:26.080
Captain, we have received
an official protest

00:16:26.115 --> 00:16:27.707
from the Romulan Empire

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:30.344
demanding the return
of your defector.

00:16:30.386 --> 00:16:33.446
Obviously, we are
refusing to comply.

00:16:33.489 --> 00:16:37.391
I join in your skepticism,
but if it is a deception

00:16:37.426 --> 00:16:41.260
the Romulans are certainly
making a good show of it.

00:16:41.297 --> 00:16:45.097
The Federation Council has
convened an emergency session.

00:16:45.134 --> 00:16:47.466
There is no doubt in my mind

00:16:47.503 --> 00:16:52.372
that this will eventually fall
on your shoulders, Jean-Luc.

00:16:52.408 --> 00:16:53.568
You've got him.

00:16:53.609 --> 00:16:56.305
You must decide
if he's telling the truth.

00:16:56.345 --> 00:17:00.748
For now, I suggest you proceed
along the Neutral Zone border

00:17:00.783 --> 00:17:04.776
toward a Federation position
proximate to Nelvana lll.

00:17:13.796 --> 00:17:15.263
Picard to Lieutenant Worf.

00:17:15.297 --> 00:17:16.594
Yes, Captain.

00:17:16.632 --> 00:17:18.930
Please come to my ready room.

00:17:18.968 --> 00:17:20.458
Aye, sir.
On my way.

00:17:22.905 --> 00:17:25.271
Slow playback.

00:17:25.307 --> 00:17:28.936
Display engine logs
and power data for both vessels.

00:17:29.044 --> 00:17:32.844
Now, watch what happens
at 095433 on the clock.

00:17:32.882 --> 00:17:34.907
The scout has sustained
engine damage

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:37.180
forcing him to slow
to.615 impulse power.

00:17:37.219 --> 00:17:40.450
The warship should overtake
him, but it doesn't.

00:17:40.489 --> 00:17:42.116
Now, just 2.6 seconds later

00:17:42.158 --> 00:17:45.457
the warship slows
to precisely the same speed.

00:17:45.494 --> 00:17:47.291
Three times,
three speed fluctuations.

00:17:47.329 --> 00:17:50.162
The warship kept its
distance every time.

00:17:50.199 --> 00:17:52.133
I don't think
they wanted to catch up.

00:17:52.168 --> 00:17:53.601
And yet they fired
on the scoutship.

00:17:53.636 --> 00:17:55.570
They could have killed him.

00:17:55.604 --> 00:17:56.901
Not necessarily, Doctor.

00:17:56.939 --> 00:17:59.567
The Romulans have
the same capability

00:17:59.608 --> 00:18:02.839
to direct the impact
of their weapons as we do.

00:18:02.878 --> 00:18:04.573
Hmm. Is there a possibility

00:18:04.613 --> 00:18:07.309
the wound could be
self-inflicted?

00:18:07.349 --> 00:18:09.544
They're very bad burns.

00:18:09.585 --> 00:18:11.246
I hardly think...

00:18:11.287 --> 00:18:13.448
A possibility.

00:18:15.291 --> 00:18:16.451
Yes.

00:18:16.492 --> 00:18:20.758
Captain's Log, Stardate 43463.7.

00:18:20.796 --> 00:18:23.788
We are holding a position
at the Neutral Zone border

00:18:23.833 --> 00:18:25.323
proximate to Nelvana lll.

00:18:25.367 --> 00:18:28.632
If our guest is telling the
truth, there are 21 hours left

00:18:28.671 --> 00:18:31.868
before the Romulan base
becomes functional.

00:18:31.907 --> 00:18:34.637
The Monitor and the Hood
are headed in your direction

00:18:34.677 --> 00:18:37.237
but they will arrive too late
to be of assistance.

00:18:37.279 --> 00:18:40.942
Warnings have gone out
to all outposts along the border

00:18:41.016 --> 00:18:44.110
as well as several independent
vessels in nearby sectors.

00:18:44.153 --> 00:18:45.950
No one here wants a war, Captain

00:18:46.055 --> 00:18:48.046
but we are prepared
to take them on

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:50.251
if that is what they want.

00:18:50.292 --> 00:18:51.919
All Federation starships

00:18:51.961 --> 00:18:54.020
have been placed
on Yellow Alert.

00:18:55.364 --> 00:18:56.888
Come.

00:18:56.932 --> 00:19:00.231
You wanted to see me, Captain?

00:19:00.269 --> 00:19:03.432
Yes, Data, I want you
to prepare a class-1 probe.

00:19:03.472 --> 00:19:05.633
Set the sensors
for maximum scan.

00:19:05.674 --> 00:19:08.734
I want every meter
of Nelvana lll monitored.

00:19:08.777 --> 00:19:11.405
I will start my calibrations,
sir.

00:19:11.447 --> 00:19:13.540
Data...

00:19:15.651 --> 00:19:18.916
Is there something else
you require of me, Captain?

00:19:18.954 --> 00:19:22.287
Your clarity of thought.

00:19:22.324 --> 00:19:26.385
Your objectivity, as always.

00:19:26.428 --> 00:19:28.089
Sit down.

00:19:30.099 --> 00:19:34.399
Data, it's very possible
that we are about to go to war.

00:19:34.436 --> 00:19:39.669
The repercussions of what we do
during the next 24 hours

00:19:39.708 --> 00:19:42.541
may be felt for years to come.

00:19:42.578 --> 00:19:46.571
I want you to keep a record
of these events

00:19:46.615 --> 00:19:49.277
so that history
will have the benefit

00:19:49.318 --> 00:19:52.344
of... a dispassionate view.

00:19:52.388 --> 00:19:53.946
I will begin immediately, sir.

00:19:54.056 --> 00:19:55.523
Is that all?

00:19:55.558 --> 00:19:57.890
How is the crew's spirit?

00:19:57.927 --> 00:19:59.622
They are concerned

00:19:59.662 --> 00:20:02.358
of course, Captain,
but confident.

00:20:02.398 --> 00:20:04.662
Do you not see that, sir?

00:20:06.702 --> 00:20:08.829
Data, unlike King Henry

00:20:08.871 --> 00:20:12.500
it is not easy for me
to disguise myself

00:20:12.541 --> 00:20:14.839
and walk among my troops.

00:20:14.877 --> 00:20:16.469
That'll be all.

00:20:29.358 --> 00:20:32.555
"Now if these men
do not die well

00:20:32.595 --> 00:20:36.429
"it will be a black matter
for the king

00:20:36.465 --> 00:20:38.490
who led them to it."

00:20:41.536 --> 00:20:44.004
Why must we waste time
playing this ridiculous game?

00:20:44.039 --> 00:20:46.166
There's more here
than you're telling us.

00:20:46.207 --> 00:20:48.175
You're forcing yourself
to hold back.

00:20:48.209 --> 00:20:50.439
I have told you
everything relevant

00:20:50.478 --> 00:20:51.775
about Nelvana lll.

00:20:51.813 --> 00:20:53.280
I'm not talking about the base.

00:20:53.314 --> 00:20:55.305
The base is all that matters.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.817
You're lying, Setal.

00:20:56.851 --> 00:20:58.751
Go to Nelvana lll
and you will see.

00:20:58.787 --> 00:21:00.914
We're not going anywhere
until we get to the truth.

00:21:00.955 --> 00:21:02.115
You're a spy, aren't you?

00:21:02.157 --> 00:21:03.124
No.

00:21:03.158 --> 00:21:04.352
Then prove it.

00:21:04.392 --> 00:21:06.587
You can begin by telling me
something about the location

00:21:06.628 --> 00:21:08.118
and the strength
of the Romulan fleet.

00:21:08.163 --> 00:21:09.061
I don't know it.

00:21:09.097 --> 00:21:10.394
You're a logistics officer.

00:21:10.432 --> 00:21:11.729
For one sector only.

00:21:11.766 --> 00:21:13.495
-Who was your superior officer?
-Admiral Jarok.

00:21:13.535 --> 00:21:14.968
The location
of the Romulan bases

00:21:15.003 --> 00:21:15.970
along the Neutral Zone?

00:21:16.071 --> 00:21:16.901
I don't know.

00:21:16.938 --> 00:21:18.462
-ln your sector?
-lrrelevant!

00:21:18.506 --> 00:21:20.269
The number of troops
under your admiral's command?

00:21:20.308 --> 00:21:23.209
Irrelevant! Irrelevant!

00:21:26.648 --> 00:21:28.445
I guess you're right.

00:21:28.483 --> 00:21:31.384
It's not worth
playing this game.

00:21:31.419 --> 00:21:33.979
Oh, what a fool I've been--

00:21:34.089 --> 00:21:39.288
to come looking for courage
in the lair of cowards.

00:21:45.066 --> 00:21:47.557
Captain Picard, priority message

00:21:47.602 --> 00:21:50.264
from Security Officer,
Klingon vessel Bortas.

00:21:50.305 --> 00:21:53.706
Mr. Worf, will you handle this
at security station, deck nine?

00:21:53.741 --> 00:21:55.003
Aye, sir.

00:21:55.076 --> 00:21:58.842
Sensors are configured
for planetary probe, sir.

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.347
Ready for launch.

00:22:00.381 --> 00:22:01.973
Proceed.

00:22:07.622 --> 00:22:09.317
Probe on course.

00:22:09.357 --> 00:22:11.951
Sensors are functioning.

00:22:11.993 --> 00:22:14.962
Coordinate your analysis
with Mr. La Forge.

00:22:14.996 --> 00:22:17.328
I want this report
with dispatch.

00:22:21.469 --> 00:22:22.436
I don't know, Data.

00:22:22.470 --> 00:22:24.461
My gut tells me
we ought to be listening

00:22:24.506 --> 00:22:26.406
to what this guy's
trying to tell us.

00:22:26.441 --> 00:22:27.533
Your "gut"?

00:22:27.575 --> 00:22:29.805
It's just a...
a feeling, you know--

00:22:29.844 --> 00:22:31.573
an instinct, intuition.

00:22:31.613 --> 00:22:33.581
But those qualities
would interfere

00:22:33.615 --> 00:22:35.879
with rational judgment,
would they not?

00:22:35.917 --> 00:22:37.612
You're right, sometimes they do.

00:22:37.652 --> 00:22:41.554
Then why not rely strictly
on the facts?

00:22:41.589 --> 00:22:44.752
Because you just can't rely
on the plain and simple facts.

00:22:44.792 --> 00:22:45.850
Sometimes they lie.

00:22:47.795 --> 00:22:50.355
They can lead
to the wrong conclusions

00:22:50.398 --> 00:22:51.865
but they cannot lie.

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:53.731
Yeah? Well, what do you think?

00:22:53.768 --> 00:22:55.599
Is he a defector or not?

00:22:55.637 --> 00:22:56.968
The facts to date would lead

00:22:57.005 --> 00:22:58.996
to the objective conclusion
that he is not.

00:22:59.073 --> 00:23:00.165
Well... somehow I think

00:23:00.208 --> 00:23:02.642
we're going to catch the
Romulans with their pants down

00:23:02.677 --> 00:23:05.669
on Nelvana lll,
just like he says.

00:23:09.284 --> 00:23:11.081
"With their pants...?"

00:23:11.119 --> 00:23:12.416
A metaphor.

00:23:12.453 --> 00:23:14.580
Catching them in the act.

00:23:14.622 --> 00:23:16.749
Because your gut tells you so.

00:23:16.791 --> 00:23:17.883
Exactly.

00:23:17.926 --> 00:23:21.123
But you can't always
go with your gut, either.

00:23:21.162 --> 00:23:22.288
It's...

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:24.890
Well, it's a combination, Data.

00:23:24.933 --> 00:23:27.128
All right, I'll put it to you
this way.

00:23:27.168 --> 00:23:30.365
All these feelings that get
in the way of human judgment

00:23:30.405 --> 00:23:32.202
that confuse the hell out of us

00:23:32.240 --> 00:23:34.333
that make us
second-guess ourselves--

00:23:34.375 --> 00:23:35.899
well, we need them.

00:23:35.944 --> 00:23:37.411
We need them to...

00:23:37.445 --> 00:23:38.912
help us fill in
the missing pieces

00:23:38.947 --> 00:23:42.212
because we almost never
have all the facts.

00:23:42.250 --> 00:23:47.688
So a person fills in
the missing pieces of the puzzle

00:23:47.722 --> 00:23:52.989
with his own personality,
resulting in a conclusion

00:23:53.027 --> 00:23:56.190
based as much
on instinct and intuition

00:23:56.231 --> 00:23:57.459
as on fact.

00:23:57.498 --> 00:23:59.125
Now you're getting it.

00:23:59.167 --> 00:24:00.327
Hmm.

00:24:02.337 --> 00:24:04.134
But what does one do

00:24:04.172 --> 00:24:07.266
if he has no instinct
or intuition?

00:24:09.477 --> 00:24:11.502
Data, look at this.

00:24:11.546 --> 00:24:14.947
The facts just took a left turn.

00:24:15.049 --> 00:24:17.916
As the probe went into
orbit around Nelvana lll

00:24:17.952 --> 00:24:21.046
it began picking up low-level
subspace radio emissions.

00:24:21.089 --> 00:24:23.421
Could they be
naturally occurring?

00:24:23.458 --> 00:24:25.653
No, sir, the patterns
are clearly artificial.

00:24:25.693 --> 00:24:26.955
The signal was so faint

00:24:27.028 --> 00:24:29.326
our ship's sensors couldn't
read it from this distance.

00:24:29.364 --> 00:24:30.763
Can we decode it?

00:24:30.798 --> 00:24:31.787
We've tried.

00:24:31.833 --> 00:24:34.097
It's probably Romulan,
but we can't be sure.

00:24:34.135 --> 00:24:36.467
We've also picked up
ionization disturbances.

00:24:36.504 --> 00:24:37.493
Cloaked Romulan ships

00:24:37.538 --> 00:24:39.870
could produce that effect.

00:24:39.907 --> 00:24:43.104
What about the planet's surface?

00:24:43.144 --> 00:24:44.941
Reading nothing but barren rock.

00:24:44.979 --> 00:24:45.968
I don't know.

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:47.945
They might be able to hide
a base from our probe.

00:24:47.982 --> 00:24:49.973
Its capabilities are limited.

00:24:50.051 --> 00:24:52.144
The only way
we'll know for sure

00:24:52.186 --> 00:24:55.280
is if we go down
and take a look for ourselves.

00:24:55.323 --> 00:24:58.451
That'll be all, gentlemen.

00:25:18.278 --> 00:25:22.715
I take it, you have never seen
a Romulan before.

00:25:22.749 --> 00:25:26.947
That would be
an incorrect assumption.

00:25:27.020 --> 00:25:30.387
Then why do you invade
my privacy?

00:25:30.423 --> 00:25:34.587
I was attempting to ascertain
what my guts tell me about you.

00:25:40.834 --> 00:25:44.167
You're the android.

00:25:44.204 --> 00:25:47.605
I know a host
of Romulan cyberneticists

00:25:47.641 --> 00:25:49.438
that would love to be

00:25:49.476 --> 00:25:50.943
this close to you.

00:25:50.977 --> 00:25:55.107
I do not find that concept
particularly appealing.

00:25:55.148 --> 00:25:57.878
Nor should you.

00:26:02.289 --> 00:26:04.257
I am told
by various crew members

00:26:04.291 --> 00:26:07.192
that this viewport is
their favorite on the ship.

00:26:07.227 --> 00:26:09.195
Hmm.

00:26:09.229 --> 00:26:14.360
I thought it would bring me
some comfort

00:26:14.401 --> 00:26:17.336
but these are not my stars.

00:26:17.370 --> 00:26:20.806
Even the heavens
are denied me here.

00:26:22.809 --> 00:26:26.438
Oh... synthetic swill.

00:26:28.448 --> 00:26:31.076
I don't suppose
your food terminals

00:26:31.117 --> 00:26:34.848
would be capable
of producing a Romulan ale?

00:26:34.888 --> 00:26:36.412
I am afraid that would require

00:26:36.456 --> 00:26:39.152
the molecular structure
of the beverage in question.

00:26:39.192 --> 00:26:40.921
And, as you are no doubt aware

00:26:40.961 --> 00:26:43.725
our knowledge of your planet
is quite limited.

00:26:43.763 --> 00:26:45.788
The loss is yours.

00:26:45.832 --> 00:26:51.464
For I have visited
over a hundred different worlds

00:26:51.504 --> 00:26:56.965
and none possessed
the awesome beauty of Romulus.

00:26:57.077 --> 00:26:58.669
Am I correct in assuming

00:26:58.712 --> 00:27:01.203
you regret your decision
to come here?

00:27:01.248 --> 00:27:05.685
What I did had to be done

00:27:05.719 --> 00:27:15.754
but... never again to see
the firefalls at Gal Gath'thong

00:27:15.795 --> 00:27:18.764
and the spires of my home

00:27:18.798 --> 00:27:23.098
as they rise
above the Apnex Sea at dawn.

00:27:23.136 --> 00:27:28.096
It's a bitter thing
to be exiled from your own home.

00:27:28.141 --> 00:27:30.268
It does appear unlikely

00:27:30.310 --> 00:27:33.871
you will ever be allowed
to return to your planet.

00:27:33.914 --> 00:27:40.649
The cold reaction of an android.

00:27:43.256 --> 00:27:46.817
But perhaps we can bring Romulus
to you.

00:27:50.730 --> 00:27:52.857
Program complete.

00:27:52.899 --> 00:27:54.890
Run program.

00:27:57.370 --> 00:27:59.031
After you.

00:28:15.855 --> 00:28:18.517
The Valley of Chula.

00:28:18.558 --> 00:28:20.549
I know it well.

00:28:20.593 --> 00:28:25.257
You are free to stay here
as long as you wish.

00:28:27.534 --> 00:28:29.934
I no longer live here.

00:28:29.970 --> 00:28:31.961
Turn it off.

00:28:35.241 --> 00:28:37.232
Cancel program.

00:28:38.878 --> 00:28:44.077
This... this is my home
now, my future.

00:28:44.117 --> 00:28:48.076
I have sacrificed everything.

00:28:48.121 --> 00:28:51.284
It must not be in vain.

00:28:51.324 --> 00:28:56.455
Arrange a meeting between
myself and Captain Picard.

00:29:01.267 --> 00:29:05.931
Tell him Admiral Jarok
wants to see him.

00:29:11.811 --> 00:29:13.802
Captain, we have confirmed

00:29:13.847 --> 00:29:17.112
that you are holding
Admiral Alidar Jarok.

00:29:17.150 --> 00:29:19.175
He has been identified
as the commander

00:29:19.219 --> 00:29:21.278
at the massacre
of the Norkan outposts.

00:29:21.321 --> 00:29:25.087
The council strongly advises
that you consider Jarok

00:29:25.125 --> 00:29:28.461
an unreliable source
of information.

00:29:34.834 --> 00:29:36.768
Bring him in.

00:29:39.238 --> 00:29:41.832
Ensign, will you wait outside?

00:29:44.844 --> 00:29:47.335
Have a seat, Admiral Jarok.

00:29:47.379 --> 00:29:50.314
Captain, there is no more time.

00:29:50.349 --> 00:29:52.340
Admiral, have a seat.

00:29:57.690 --> 00:30:03.651
You see, I'm just not convinced
that you are telling the truth.

00:30:03.696 --> 00:30:05.687
What must I do?

00:30:05.731 --> 00:30:08.598
You must convince me.

00:30:08.634 --> 00:30:13.071
If I had irrefutable evidence...

00:30:13.105 --> 00:30:15.938
but you did not bring
irrefutable evidence.

00:30:15.975 --> 00:30:17.533
You brought no evidence at all.

00:30:17.576 --> 00:30:21.842
And now I hear you are not
the man you claimed to be.

00:30:21.881 --> 00:30:23.143
Admiral...

00:30:23.182 --> 00:30:27.278
your credibility
is stretched beyond belief.

00:30:27.319 --> 00:30:32.621
A Romulan defector is almost
a contradiction in terms

00:30:32.658 --> 00:30:35.684
but Admiral Jarok
crossing the lines?

00:30:35.728 --> 00:30:39.994
I explained my motivations
to your interrogators.

00:30:40.099 --> 00:30:43.330
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes--
peace in our galaxy.

00:30:43.369 --> 00:30:46.202
Except, Admiral,
you are not a man of peace.

00:30:46.238 --> 00:30:49.605
Your military record,
what we know of it, is clear.

00:30:49.642 --> 00:30:53.874
Which is precisely why I chose
an alternate identity here.

00:30:53.913 --> 00:30:57.371
The massacres in the Norkan
outposts, for example.

00:30:57.416 --> 00:31:01.648
What you call "massacres"
were called

00:31:01.687 --> 00:31:06.818
the "Norkan campaigns"
on my world, Captain.

00:31:06.859 --> 00:31:11.489
One world's butcher
is another world's hero.

00:31:11.530 --> 00:31:14.294
Perhaps I am neither one.

00:31:17.536 --> 00:31:22.166
On what basis, Admiral,
am I to decide?

00:31:22.207 --> 00:31:23.868
Hmm?

00:31:26.211 --> 00:31:28.111
Your good word?

00:31:28.147 --> 00:31:30.843
Are you willing
to help us overpower

00:31:30.883 --> 00:31:34.478
the Romulan B-Type warbirds
we may encounter?

00:31:34.520 --> 00:31:37.648
Are you prepared
to help us detect them

00:31:37.690 --> 00:31:40.215
through their cloaking shields?

00:31:42.561 --> 00:31:46.793
Well, you see my problem,
Admiral.

00:31:46.832 --> 00:31:49.960
You ask us for faith

00:31:50.002 --> 00:31:53.529
in circumstances which are
hardly possible to believe

00:31:53.572 --> 00:31:56.632
compounded by lies
and your refusal to tell us

00:31:56.675 --> 00:31:57.664
what you know.

00:31:57.710 --> 00:32:00.008
I cannot betray my people.

00:32:00.045 --> 00:32:02.138
You've already betrayed
your people, Admiral.

00:32:02.181 --> 00:32:04.274
You've made your choices, sir.

00:32:04.316 --> 00:32:05.510
You're a traitor.

00:32:05.551 --> 00:32:09.317
Now, if the bitter taste of that
is unpalatable to you

00:32:09.355 --> 00:32:12.483
I am truly sorry,
but I will not risk my crew

00:32:12.524 --> 00:32:17.052
because you think you can dance
on the edge of the Neutral Zone.

00:32:17.096 --> 00:32:20.463
You've crossed over, Admiral.

00:32:20.499 --> 00:32:24.629
You make yourself comfortable
with that.

00:32:26.739 --> 00:32:31.676
Do you... have any children,
Captain Picard, a family?

00:32:31.710 --> 00:32:34.474
No.

00:32:34.513 --> 00:32:40.975
Oh. Then you have sacrificed
too much for your career.

00:32:41.086 --> 00:32:44.180
Yes, this is all
very interesting...

00:32:44.223 --> 00:32:46.919
There comes a time
in a man's life

00:32:46.959 --> 00:32:48.620
that you cannot know

00:32:48.661 --> 00:32:53.530
when he looks down at the first
smile of his baby girl

00:32:53.565 --> 00:32:57.797
and realizes he must change
the world for her--

00:32:57.836 --> 00:33:00.634
for all children.

00:33:00.673 --> 00:33:03.801
It is for her that I am here.

00:33:03.842 --> 00:33:09.178
Not to destroy the Romulan
Empire, but to save it.

00:33:09.214 --> 00:33:11.409
For months

00:33:11.450 --> 00:33:15.477
I tried desperately
to persuade the High Command

00:33:15.521 --> 00:33:18.888
that another war
would destroy the Empire.

00:33:18.924 --> 00:33:20.824
They got tired of my arguments.

00:33:20.859 --> 00:33:22.918
Finally, I was censured

00:33:22.961 --> 00:33:26.488
sent off to command
some distant sector.

00:33:26.532 --> 00:33:29.524
This was my only recourse.

00:33:31.203 --> 00:33:33.501
I...

00:33:33.539 --> 00:33:39.136
will never see
my child smile again.

00:33:39.178 --> 00:33:41.976
She will grow up believing

00:33:42.081 --> 00:33:46.677
that her father is a traitor.

00:33:46.719 --> 00:33:50.120
But she will grow up...

00:33:50.155 --> 00:33:56.151
if you act, Picard, if we stop
this war before it begins.

00:33:56.195 --> 00:34:00.256
I can't and I won't

00:34:00.299 --> 00:34:05.134
unless I have
unequivocal cooperation.

00:34:21.854 --> 00:34:27.884
Admiral Jarok has provided me
with the locations, strengths

00:34:27.926 --> 00:34:31.487
and tactical plans
of the Romulan fleet.

00:34:31.530 --> 00:34:34.158
Mr. La Forge, he is prepared

00:34:34.199 --> 00:34:37.965
to give you data
regarding engines

00:34:38.070 --> 00:34:40.197
weapons,
and the cloaking systems

00:34:40.239 --> 00:34:42.764
of the warbird class starship.

00:34:42.808 --> 00:34:44.173
But I believe

00:34:44.209 --> 00:34:47.372
his experience as a field
commander will be more valuable

00:34:47.412 --> 00:34:50.347
for its strategic sense
than in the technical areas.

00:34:50.382 --> 00:34:52.316
Any edge will help, Captain.

00:34:52.351 --> 00:34:53.318
Don't depend on this.

00:34:53.352 --> 00:34:54.785
For all we know,
he may be still lying

00:34:54.820 --> 00:34:56.447
but we shall find that out
soon enough.

00:34:56.488 --> 00:34:57.455
Number One

00:34:57.489 --> 00:34:59.719
set course for Nelvana lll.

00:35:04.962 --> 00:35:09.262
Second Officer's Log,
Stardate 43465.2.

00:35:09.300 --> 00:35:11.200
We have entered the Neutral Zone

00:35:11.235 --> 00:35:13.897
in direct violation
of the Treaty of Algeron.

00:35:13.938 --> 00:35:17.271
Presuming Romulan warships
are cloaked and monitoring us

00:35:17.308 --> 00:35:18.866
we expect heavy resistance

00:35:18.910 --> 00:35:20.775
as we approach Nelvana lll.

00:35:20.812 --> 00:35:21.779
Tactical?

00:35:21.813 --> 00:35:23.110
Nothing on sensors.

00:35:23.147 --> 00:35:24.205
I don't like it.

00:35:24.248 --> 00:35:26.910
I would have expected
a greeting party.

00:35:26.951 --> 00:35:29.613
You echo
another noteworthy commander

00:35:29.654 --> 00:35:32.384
in similar circumstances,
Number One.

00:35:32.423 --> 00:35:34.653
A countryman of yours--

00:35:34.692 --> 00:35:36.216
George Armstrong Custer

00:35:36.260 --> 00:35:39.923
when his Seventh Cavalry
arrived at The Little Bighorn.

00:35:39.964 --> 00:35:41.693
May we have better luck.

00:35:41.732 --> 00:35:43.632
Approaching Nelvana system.

00:35:43.668 --> 00:35:46.102
Engage impulse engines.

00:35:50.842 --> 00:35:52.776
Nelvana lll on screen.

00:35:59.383 --> 00:36:02.011
Still no signs of them
on sensors.

00:36:02.053 --> 00:36:05.489
In a way, I'd rather be fighting
my way through this.

00:36:05.523 --> 00:36:07.150
It's just too damned easy.

00:36:07.191 --> 00:36:09.557
Prepare to enter standard orbit.

00:36:15.733 --> 00:36:16.700
Data?

00:36:16.734 --> 00:36:18.895
Scanning the planet, sir.

00:36:18.936 --> 00:36:22.394
No life forms, no power sources,
no weapons systems.

00:36:22.440 --> 00:36:24.533
No indication of a base at all?

00:36:24.575 --> 00:36:26.042
No, sir.

00:36:26.077 --> 00:36:28.477
The subspace signal
the probe detected?

00:36:28.513 --> 00:36:29.810
The ionization disturbances?

00:36:29.847 --> 00:36:32.111
I am picking them up, sir

00:36:32.149 --> 00:36:34.413
but I cannot identify
the source.

00:36:34.452 --> 00:36:37.751
They seem to be moving
in an orbital path

00:36:37.788 --> 00:36:40.518
with an 800-kilometer apogee.

00:36:43.895 --> 00:36:46.523
Lieutenant Worf,
bring the Admiral up here.

00:36:46.564 --> 00:36:47.997
Aye, sir.

00:36:51.536 --> 00:36:54.835
Maybe they abandoned the planet
after he defected.

00:36:54.872 --> 00:36:56.965
There is no scarring
on the planet surface

00:36:57.074 --> 00:36:59.634
that would denote heavy
construction of any kind.

00:36:59.677 --> 00:37:02.646
A cloaking device of some sort
to hide the entire base?

00:37:02.680 --> 00:37:05.240
A cloaking device
operating on the surface

00:37:05.283 --> 00:37:07.945
would be given away
by visible distortion effects.

00:37:13.958 --> 00:37:16.085
Perhaps you would care
to explain

00:37:16.127 --> 00:37:17.822
why we are here, Admiral.

00:37:17.862 --> 00:37:21.161
There doesn't appear
to be a base.

00:37:25.236 --> 00:37:26.533
I don't understand.

00:37:26.571 --> 00:37:28.095
Nelvana lll, Admiral!

00:37:28.139 --> 00:37:29.106
No base!

00:37:29.140 --> 00:37:30.368
No weapons!

00:37:30.408 --> 00:37:32.603
No sign of any life at all!

00:37:38.049 --> 00:37:42.645
I-I saw
the tactical communiques--

00:37:42.687 --> 00:37:46.953
the records,
timetables for completion.

00:37:47.024 --> 00:37:50.721
An entire legion
was assigned to this section.

00:37:50.761 --> 00:37:54.993
Is it possible they could have
been feeding you disinformation?

00:37:58.703 --> 00:38:00.796
You said
that you had been censured--

00:38:00.838 --> 00:38:03.329
reassigned four months ago.

00:38:03.374 --> 00:38:05.342
They knew
of your dissatisfaction.

00:38:05.376 --> 00:38:09.437
Could all this have been
to test your loyalty?

00:38:09.480 --> 00:38:12.677
No.

00:38:12.717 --> 00:38:15.151
No!

00:38:15.186 --> 00:38:17.211
It's impossible.

00:38:27.565 --> 00:38:30.193
They let you escape

00:38:30.234 --> 00:38:33.101
with an arsenal
of worthless secrets.

00:38:33.137 --> 00:38:36.334
What other explanation
is there?

00:38:36.374 --> 00:38:38.342
Permission to withdraw
from the Neutral Zone.

00:38:38.376 --> 00:38:39.934
At your earliest convenience,
Number One.

00:38:40.044 --> 00:38:42.274
Helm, bring her around
180 degrees!

00:38:42.313 --> 00:38:44.804
Geordi, get us out of here!

00:38:44.849 --> 00:38:47.017
I hear you, Commander.

00:38:54.858 --> 00:38:56.485
Two Romulan warships uncloaking.

00:38:56.526 --> 00:38:58.687
Coordinates...

00:39:06.302 --> 00:39:07.530
Shields holding.

00:39:07.570 --> 00:39:08.696
Damage?

00:39:08.738 --> 00:39:10.296
Minor damage
to the secondary hull.

00:39:10.340 --> 00:39:12.604
Power transfer fields
may be pinched off.

00:39:12.642 --> 00:39:14.906
I'm working on it.

00:39:15.011 --> 00:39:16.342
Captain?

00:39:16.379 --> 00:39:18.347
Not yet, Mr. Worf.

00:39:18.381 --> 00:39:20.849
This is just a tap
on the shoulder

00:39:20.884 --> 00:39:23.614
or we wouldn't be here
talking about it.

00:39:23.653 --> 00:39:25.678
The Romulans are hailing us.

00:39:25.722 --> 00:39:27.280
On screen.

00:39:27.323 --> 00:39:29.154
Captain Picard

00:39:29.192 --> 00:39:32.753
I hardly expected
to see you again so soon.

00:39:32.796 --> 00:39:35.321
It seems this time
you are the one

00:39:35.365 --> 00:39:38.664
who has made an aggressive move
across the Neutral Zone.

00:39:38.701 --> 00:39:41.932
Commander Tomalak,
as I am sure you already know

00:39:41.971 --> 00:39:43.939
we were responding to warnings

00:39:43.973 --> 00:39:46.464
of Romulan incursions
at Nelvana lll.

00:39:46.509 --> 00:39:51.742
But, Captain, as you can see,
there is no incursion.

00:39:51.781 --> 00:39:54.079
And the matter
of the unidentified

00:39:54.117 --> 00:39:57.814
subspace radio emissions
and the ionization disturbances?

00:39:57.854 --> 00:40:01.813
Oh, you must mean
our orbiting probe.

00:40:01.858 --> 00:40:07.797
We are studying Nelvana lll
for... archaeological research.

00:40:07.831 --> 00:40:10.800
With a cloaked satellite?

00:40:10.834 --> 00:40:13.462
Oh, really, Captain,
would you have us believe

00:40:13.503 --> 00:40:15.971
this satellite is an excuse

00:40:16.039 --> 00:40:18.633
for your aggressive charge
across the Neutral Zone?

00:40:18.675 --> 00:40:20.836
You can believe what you wish

00:40:20.877 --> 00:40:22.970
and we will be on our way.

00:40:23.079 --> 00:40:25.775
Without even an apology,
Captain?

00:40:25.815 --> 00:40:29.376
If an apology will do,
then I offer it.

00:40:29.419 --> 00:40:30.579
I'm afraid it won't

00:40:30.620 --> 00:40:33.214
so I will save you
the humiliation.

00:40:33.256 --> 00:40:35.190
Get to it, Tomalak!

00:40:35.225 --> 00:40:39.093
You see, Picard,
after we dissect your Enterprise

00:40:39.129 --> 00:40:41.859
for every precious bit
of information

00:40:41.898 --> 00:40:44.560
I intend to display
its broken hull

00:40:44.601 --> 00:40:46.535
in the center
of the Romulan capitol

00:40:46.569 --> 00:40:48.093
as a symbol of our victory.

00:40:48.138 --> 00:40:51.630
It will inspire our armies
for generations to come

00:40:51.674 --> 00:40:54.234
and serve as a warning
to any other traitor

00:40:54.277 --> 00:40:56.643
who would create ripples
of disloyalty.

00:41:01.918 --> 00:41:06.821
All the communiques,
all the timetables

00:41:06.856 --> 00:41:10.314
all the records--
they were all fiction

00:41:10.360 --> 00:41:12.191
written for my benefit.

00:41:12.228 --> 00:41:13.855
A test...

00:41:13.897 --> 00:41:17.230
a test of my loyalty.

00:41:17.267 --> 00:41:21.226
And you used me
to lure the Enterprise

00:41:21.271 --> 00:41:23.569
into the Neutral Zone.

00:41:23.606 --> 00:41:29.567
First, Captain, you will
return the traitor, Jarok.

00:41:29.612 --> 00:41:33.412
Then you will surrender
as prisoners of war.

00:41:33.449 --> 00:41:36.316
Do you seriously expect me
to accept those terms?

00:41:36.352 --> 00:41:42.848
No, Captain Picard,
I expect you won't.

00:41:42.892 --> 00:41:46.589
You have 30 seconds to decide.

00:41:46.629 --> 00:41:48.927
I do not require one, Tomalak.

00:41:48.965 --> 00:41:53.800
I urge you, Captain Picard--
surrender.

00:41:53.836 --> 00:41:56.805
Consider the men and women
you would lead

00:41:56.839 --> 00:41:59.330
into a lost cause.

00:42:02.645 --> 00:42:06.604
If the cause is just
and honorable

00:42:06.649 --> 00:42:09.243
they are prepared
to give their lives.

00:42:09.285 --> 00:42:11.947
Are you prepared
to die today, Tomalak?

00:42:12.021 --> 00:42:17.323
I expected more from you
than an idle threat, Picard.

00:42:17.360 --> 00:42:20.352
Then you shall have it.

00:42:20.396 --> 00:42:21.954
Mr. Worf.

00:42:22.031 --> 00:42:24.795
Aye, sir.

00:42:32.675 --> 00:42:35.143
Klingon warships--
armed and ready, sir.

00:42:38.581 --> 00:42:41.277
What shall it be, Tomalak?

00:42:41.317 --> 00:42:45.378
You will still not survive
our assault.

00:42:45.421 --> 00:42:48.481
And you will not survive ours.

00:42:48.524 --> 00:42:50.583
Shall we die together?

00:42:53.596 --> 00:42:57.896
I look forward
to our next meeting, Captain.

00:43:01.004 --> 00:43:04.440
Romulan disrupters
are powering down, sir.

00:43:09.312 --> 00:43:12.907
Cancel Red Alert.

00:43:14.917 --> 00:43:16.612
Mr. Worf, will you extend

00:43:16.653 --> 00:43:18.951
the appreciation
of the Federation

00:43:19.055 --> 00:43:21.888
and my personal gratitude
to the Klingons.

00:43:21.924 --> 00:43:23.915
Aye, sir.

00:43:23.960 --> 00:43:29.364
Take us back, Number One.

00:43:29.399 --> 00:43:33.802
I did it for nothing.

00:43:33.836 --> 00:43:38.398
My home, my family...

00:43:38.441 --> 00:43:40.739
for nothing.

00:43:51.888 --> 00:43:53.981
He ingested a Felodesine chip.

00:43:54.057 --> 00:43:55.991
He must have
brought it with him.

00:43:56.092 --> 00:44:00.153
I'm sorry, Captain,
there was no antidote.

00:44:00.196 --> 00:44:04.690
A letter to his wife
and daughter.

00:44:04.734 --> 00:44:08.431
Sir, he must have known
it would be impossible

00:44:08.471 --> 00:44:12.237
for us to deliver it.

00:44:12.275 --> 00:44:14.266
Today, perhaps

00:44:14.310 --> 00:44:16.278
but if there are others

00:44:16.312 --> 00:44:18.644
with the courage
of Admiral Jarok

00:44:18.681 --> 00:44:23.380
we may hope to see
a day of peace

00:44:23.419 --> 00:44:28.158
when we can
take his letter home.
